        en: "'A dike is really a very long hill,' Farmer Jan explains. 'The inside is made of sand. On top of that lies a thick layer of clay. Clay is sticky and lets almost no water through. Grass grows on top, and the roots hold the soil firmly together.' On the sea side there are often large stones as well. They break the waves, so that the water cannot wash the dike away.",
