        en: "Who actually looks after all those dikes? The water board does. It is one of the oldest forms of government in the Netherlands, more than eight hundred years old. Water board staff regularly walk along the dikes to check for cracks, holes or wet patches. Especially after a storm they are extra careful. After all, a small leak can quickly become a big problem.",
