        en: "The most famous dike in the Netherlands is the Afsluitdijk. It is more than thirty kilometres long and was finished in 1932. It separates the Wadden Sea from the IJsselmeer. In Zeeland you find the Delta Works: huge dams and storm surge barriers. The Eastern Scheldt barrier has gates that only close when a severe storm is coming. That way seawater can normally flow in and out, and fish and birds can simply go on living there.",
