        en: "'Will the dikes get even higher?' asks Sam. Farmer Jan nods. Because the earth is getting warmer, the sea level is rising very slowly. And sometimes it rains much harder than it used to. That is why engineers are always working on new plans. They make dikes wider and stronger, and sometimes they actually give a river more room. Then a meadow is allowed to flood for a while at high water, so that the towns stay dry.",
