        en: "Then something unbelievable happened. Out of every cellar, every attic and every cupboard came rats. Big rats, small rats, grey rats and brown rats. They ran after the piper, as if they were bewitched. The man walked out through the town gate, to the bank of the Weser. There he waded into the water up to his knees. The rats followed him, and the current carried them all away. Hamelin was saved.",
