        en: "People danced in the streets for joy. But when the piper came to collect his thousand gold coins, the mayor laughed at him. 'A thousand coins for a little tune on a pipe? The rats are gone anyway. Here are fifty, and be glad of them.' The piper looked at him long and seriously. 'You have broken your word,' he said quietly. 'You will be sorry for that.' Then he turned round and disappeared.",
