        en: "Hansje hurried home along the dike. On one side lay the meadows with the cows, on the other side the water lapped high against the stones. It had rained all week and the water was higher than normal. Hansje picked a few flowers for his mother and hummed a tune. Suddenly he stopped dead. He heard a sound that did not belong there: a soft, trickling splash.",
